# Customer Churn & Retention Analysis

## Project Overview

Customer churn is a major challenge for subscription-based businesses. This project analyzes customer data to identify churn patterns, understand the factors associated with customer attrition, and uncover opportunities to improve customer retention.

The project uses Python for data cleaning and exploratory analysis, SQL (MySQL) for data analysis, and Power BI for interactive visualization.

## Business Objectives

- Measure overall customer churn and retention rates.
- Analyze churn across contract types and customer tenure.
- Investigate the relationship between monthly charges and churn.
- Identify payment methods associated with higher churn.
- Compare churn rates across internet service types.
- Present actionable insights through a Power BI dashboard.

## Tools & Technologies

- **Python:** Data cleaning, transformation, and exploratory data analysis
- **Pandas:** Data manipulation and aggregation
- **SQL (MySQL):** Overall churn calculation and churn analysis by contract type, tenure, monthly charges, payment method, and internet service
- **Power BI:** Interactive dashboard and KPI visualization
- **CSV:** Dataset storage and analysis outputs

## Dataset

The project uses the Telco Customer Churn dataset, which contains customer information, subscription details, payment methods, service usage, charges, and churn status.

Python analysis results:

- **Total customer records:** 7,043
- **Churned customers:** 1,869
- **Retained customers:** 5,174

The SQL analysis uses 7,032 imported records because 11 records with blank `TotalCharges` values were skipped during import.

## Key Performance Indicators

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Total Customers | 7,043 |
| Churned Customers | 1,869 |
| Retained Customers | 5,174 |
| Overall Churn Rate | 26.54% |
| Overall Retention Rate | 73.46% |

## Key Findings

### 1. Contract Type

| Contract | Churn Rate |
|---|---:|
| Month-to-month | 42.71% |
| One year | 11.27% |
| Two year | 2.83% |

Month-to-month customers have the highest churn rate, while customers on two-year contracts have the lowest.

### 2. Customer Tenure

| Tenure Group | Churn Rate |
|---|---:|
| 0–12 months | 47.44% |
| 13–24 months | 28.71% |
| 25–48 months | 20.39% |
| 49–72 months | 9.51% |

Churn is highest among customers in their first year and generally declines as tenure increases.

### 3. Monthly Charges

| Monthly Charges | Churn Rate |
|---|---:|
| 0–35 | 10.89% |
| 35–65 | 23.14% |
| 65–90 | 36.30% |
| 90–120 | 32.78% |

Customers in the 65–90 monthly charge group have the highest churn rate among the analyzed charge segments.

### 4. Payment Method

| Payment Method | Churn Rate |
|---|---:|
| Electronic check | 45.29% |
| Mailed check | 19.11% |
| Bank transfer (automatic) | 16.71% |
| Credit card (automatic) | 15.24% |

Customers using electronic checks have a substantially higher churn rate than customers using the other payment methods.

### 5. Internet Service

| Internet Service | Churn Rate |
|---|---:|
| Fiber optic | 41.89% |
| DSL | 19.00% |
| No internet service | 7.43% |

Customers using fiber-optic internet have a higher observed churn rate than customers using DSL or no internet service. Further analysis could investigate whether pricing, service quality, or customer characteristics contribute to this difference.

## Business Recommendations

Based on the analysis, the following actions could help improve retention:

- **Strengthen early customer engagement:** Introduce onboarding support and proactive follow-ups during the first 12 months.
- **Encourage longer contracts:** Test loyalty benefits and incentives for customers considering annual or multi-year plans.
- **Review pricing and value perception:** Investigate whether customers with higher monthly charges feel they receive sufficient value.
- **Investigate electronic-check churn:** Explore payment friction, customer preferences, and potential differences in customer profiles.
- **Review fiber-optic customer experience:** Investigate service quality, pricing, and customer satisfaction among fiber-optic subscribers.
- **Monitor churn KPIs:** Track churn rate by tenure, contract, payment method, internet service, and monthly charge segment over time.

These recommendations are based on observed associations in the dataset; they do not establish that any individual factor directly causes churn.

## SQL Analysis

SQL queries are available in [`sql/churn_analysis.sql`](sql/churn_analysis.sql).

The queries cover:

- Overall customer count, churned customers, retained customers, and churn rate
- Churn analysis by contract type
- Churn analysis by tenure group
- Churn analysis by monthly charge group
- Churn analysis by payment method
- Churn analysis by internet service

## Power BI Dashboard

![Customer Churn & Retention Analysis Dashboard](screenshots/Customer_Churn%20Report.png)
The interactive dashboard includes:

- Total customer, churn, and retention KPIs
- Churn by contract type
- Churn by tenure group
- Churn by payment method
- Churn by monthly charge group
- Customer churn distribution
- Churn by internet service
- Interactive slicers for customer segmentation

